#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting {#troubleshooting}"
msgstr "Pag-troubleshoot {#troubleshooting}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`winget` is not recognized\">\n"
"Update the [App Installer](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9nblggh4nns1) from the Microsoft Store, or use the relevant manual download links\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`cl` is not recognized\">\n"
"Rerun the MSVC load cell (Step 3), or use the x64 Native Tools Command Prompt\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`python` opens Microsoft Store\">\n"
"Go to Settings → Apps → Advanced app settings → App execution aliases and turn off `python.exe`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`.ps1 cannot be loaded` / scripts disabled\">\n"
"Run `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned` then retry\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`cannot open file 'qiskit.h'`\">\n"
"Run `python -c \"import qiskit.capi; print(qiskit.capi.get_include())\"` and confirm the path exists\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`qiskit.capi` not found\">\n"
"Run `pip install \"qiskit[visualization]~=2.4.2\"`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`qiskit-aer` build fails\">\n"
"Run `pip install qiskit-aer --only-binary=:all:`. If that also fails, use Python 3.12 or skip aer, which is optional\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Build runs but import fails with a version error\">\n"
"The built Qiskit C extension and the installed Qiskit version must have the same version.  Reinstall Qiskit with `pip install \"qiskit~=2.4.2\"`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"I rebuilt the C but the circuit did not change\">\n"
"A C extension cannot be re-imported live. Restart the kernel, rerun the MSVC commands (Step 3), then rebuild\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"PowerShell script was blocked\">\n"
"`Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Path length errors\">\n"
"Use a short root path on C:\\ (for example, `C:\\workspace`, or the path you set in the setup step), or enable Long Paths: Settings → System → For developers → Long Paths\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Conda is active (the prompt shows `(base)`) or builds behave oddly after using Anaconda\">\n"
"Run `conda deactivate` until `CONDA_DEFAULT_ENV` and `CONDA_PREFIX` are both gone from the environment. Check with `$env:CONDA_PREFIX`. If they persist, open a fresh PowerShell (not an Anaconda prompt) and retry from Step 2.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"The virtual environment was created from a conda-managed Python (check the `home =` line in `.venv\\pyvenv.cfg`)\">\n"
"The virtual environment inherited conda's C runtime and cannot be fixed in place. Delete it, download Python 3.12 from the [Python](https://www.python.org/downloads/) website, and rebuild. Run `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .venv`, then rerun the Python detection snippet in Step 1 to set `$PYTHON_EXE`, then recreate the virtual environment (Step 2).\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`DLL load failed` on import\">\n"
"Conda is likely leaking into the virtual environment. Check both of the issues immediately above this. Also verify that Python is 64-bit: `python -c \"import platform; print(platform.architecture())\"`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Build fails with garbled paths or `C1083`\">\n"
"Your username or workspace path contains non-ASCII characters. Move the workspace to a short ASCII-only path (for example, `C:\\workspace`)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Build or import randomly fails, works on retry\">\n"
"The workspace folder is synced by OneDrive. Move it to a local path like `C:\\workspace`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Build interrupted midway (for example, there was a power loss)\">\n"
"Delete the `_smoke_pkg` folder in your workspace, rerun the MSVC load cell, then rerun the smoke test cell\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`pip install` fails with SSL certificate error\">\n"
"Your network uses a proxy that intercepts HTTPS. Try running `pip install --trusted-host pypi.org --trusted-host files.pythonhosted.org qiskit` or ask your network administrator for the proxy CA certificate\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Windows Defender quarantines the `.pyd` file\">\n"
"Add your workspace's `.venv` and `_smoke_pkg` folders to Defender exclusions by going to Windows Security → Virus & threat protection → Manage settings → Exclusions\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"VS Build Tools cannot be installed (no admin rights)\">\n"
"Administrator access is required. Ask your IT department for access\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`WinError 32` / file in use during rebuild\">\n"
"The .pyd is locked by the running kernel. Restart the kernel (Ctrl+Shift+P → Jupyter: Restart Kernel), rerun Step 3, then rebuild\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Commands silently do nothing (no error, no output)\">\n"
"You might be in cmd.exe instead of PowerShell. Check your prompt: PowerShell shows `PS C:\\>`, cmd shows `C:\\>`. Open PowerShell from Start Menu or Win+X\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"MSVC install appears stuck\">\n"
"The `--passive --wait` flags block PowerShell while the installer runs in the background. Check your taskbar for a \"Visual Studio Installer\" window. It can take 10-30 minutes to install\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Hindi nakikilala ang `winget`\">\n"
"I-update ang [App Installer](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9nblggh4nns1) mula sa Microsoft Store, o gamitin ang kaugnay na mga manual na link sa pag-download\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Hindi nakikilala ang `cl`\">\n"
"Patakbuhin ulit ang MSVC load cell (Hakbang 3), o gamitin ang x64 Native Tools Command Prompt\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Binubuksan ng `python` ang Microsoft Store\">\n"
"Pumunta sa Settings → Apps → Advanced app settings → App execution aliases at i-off ang `python.exe`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`.ps1 cannot be loaded` / naka-disable ang mga script\">\n"
"Patakbuhin ang `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned` pagkatapos ay subukan ulit\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`cannot open file 'qiskit.h'`\">\n"
"Patakbuhin ang `python -c \"import qiskit.capi; print(qiskit.capi.get_include())\"` at kumpirmahin na umiiral ang path\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Hindi mahanap ang `qiskit.capi`\">\n"
"Patakbuhin ang `pip install \"qiskit[visualization]~=2.4.2\"`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Nabigo ang build ng `qiskit-aer`\">\n"
"Patakbuhin ang `pip install qiskit-aer --only-binary=:all:`. Kung nabigo rin iyon, gamitin ang Python 3.12 o laktawan ang aer, na opsyonal\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tumatakbo ang build ngunit nabigo ang import dahil sa version error\">\n"
"Ang binuong Qiskit C extension at ang na-install na bersyon ng Qiskit ay dapat magkaparehong bersyon.  I-reinstall ang Qiskit gamit ang `pip install \"qiskit~=2.4.2\"`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Muli kong binuo ang C ngunit hindi nagbago ang circuit\">\n"
"Hindi maaaring i-re-import nang live ang isang C extension. I-restart ang kernel, patakbuhin ulit ang mga MSVC command (Hakbang 3), pagkatapos ay muling buuin\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Na-block ang PowerShell script\">\n"
"`Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mga error sa haba ng path\">\n"
"Gumamit ng maikling root path sa C:\\ (halimbawa, `C:\\workspace`, o ang path na itinakda mo sa hakbang ng setup), o paganahin ang Long Paths: Settings → System → For developers → Long Paths\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Aktibo ang Conda (ipinapakita ng prompt ang `(base)`) o kakaiba ang kilos ng mga build pagkatapos gumamit ng Anaconda\">\n"
"Patakbuhin ang `conda deactivate` hanggang mawala ang parehong `CONDA_DEFAULT_ENV` at `CONDA_PREFIX` mula sa environment. Suriin gamit ang `$env:CONDA_PREFIX`. Kung nagpapatuloy pa rin ang mga ito, magbukas ng bagong PowerShell (hindi Anaconda prompt) at subukan ulit mula sa Hakbang 2.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Ginawa ang virtual environment mula sa isang conda-managed na Python (tingnan ang linyang `home =` sa `.venv\\pyvenv.cfg`)\">\n"
"Namana ng virtual environment ang C runtime ng conda at hindi ito maaaring ayusin sa lugar. Burahin ito, i-download ang Python 3.12 mula sa [Python](https://www.python.org/downloads/) website, at muling buuin. Patakbuhin ang `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .venv`, pagkatapos ay patakbuhin ulit ang Python detection snippet sa Hakbang 1 upang itakda ang `$PYTHON_EXE`, pagkatapos ay gawin ulit ang virtual environment (Hakbang 2).\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`DLL load failed` sa import\">\n"
"Malamang na tumatagas ang Conda sa virtual environment. Suriin ang dalawang isyu na kasunod nito sa itaas. I-verify din na 64-bit ang Python: `python -c \"import platform; print(platform.architecture())\"`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Nabigo ang build na may sirang mga path o `C1083`\">\n"
"Naglalaman ang iyong username o workspace path ng mga non-ASCII na character. Ilipat ang workspace sa maikling ASCII-only na path (halimbawa, `C:\\workspace`)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Random na nabibigo ang build o import, gumagana sa muling pagsubok\">\n"
"Naka-sync ang workspace folder gamit ang OneDrive. Ilipat ito sa lokal na path tulad ng `C:\\workspace`\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Naantala ang build sa gitna (halimbawa, nagkaroon ng power loss)\">\n"
"Burahin ang `_smoke_pkg` folder sa iyong workspace, patakbuhin ulit ang MSVC load cell, pagkatapos ay patakbuhin ulit ang smoke test cell\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Nabigo ang `pip install` dahil sa SSL certificate error\">\n"
"Gumagamit ang iyong network ng proxy na humaharang sa HTTPS. Subukang patakbuhin ang `pip install --trusted-host pypi.org --trusted-host files.pythonhosted.org qiskit` o hilingin sa iyong network administrator ang proxy CA certificate\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Kina-quarantine ng Windows Defender ang `.pyd` file\">\n"
"Idagdag ang `.venv` at `_smoke_pkg` folder ng iyong workspace sa Defender exclusions sa pamamagitan ng pagpunta sa Windows Security → Virus & threat protection → Manage settings → Exclusions\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Hindi ma-install ang VS Build Tools (walang admin rights)\">\n"
"Kinakailangan ang administrator access. Hilingin sa iyong IT department ang access\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`WinError 32` / ginagamit ang file habang muling binubuo\">\n"
"Naka-lock ang .pyd ng tumatakbong kernel. I-restart ang kernel (Ctrl+Shift+P → Jupyter: Restart Kernel), patakbuhin ulit ang Hakbang 3, pagkatapos ay muling buuin\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tahimik na walang ginagawa ang mga command (walang error, walang output)\">\n"
"Maaaring nasa cmd.exe ka sa halip na PowerShell. Suriin ang iyong prompt: ipinapakita ng PowerShell ang `PS C:\\>`, ipinapakita ng cmd ang `C:\\>`. Buksan ang PowerShell mula sa Start Menu o Win+X\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mukhang natigil ang pag-install ng MSVC\">\n"
"Hinaharang ng mga flag na `--passive --wait` ang PowerShell habang tumatakbo ang installer sa background. Suriin ang iyong taskbar para sa isang \"Visual Studio Installer\" na window. Maaaring umabot ng 10-30 minuto ang pag-install\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

